# CHANGES -- what the game tells players has changed (src/changes.c).
# Each entry: a line '@ <id> <yyyy-mm-dd>', its text, then a blank line.
# Newest first. Ids never change and are never reused: a character's
# view counts are kept by id. Write entries for players. A change only
# staff can use gets ' staff' after the date ('@ <id> <date> staff'):
# only staff are shown it.

@ 20261030a 2026-10-30
A skill typed by its whole name now works: EGO WHIP, FISTS OF FURY,
CRANE DANCE, STUNNING BLOW, NERVE DAMAGE, STEEL FIST, DIRT KICKING,
BLINDING FISTS and the rest no longer take the rest of the name for a
target, and PICK LOCK DOOR picks the door. LOOK AT <thing> works like
LOOK <thing>.

@ 20261029b 2026-10-29
A Hyrule chest refills at every reset, but you can no longer take a
Triforce shard you already hold from it: one of each is all the
Triforce needs. A spare already in your pack is taken back when you
next log in.

@ 20261029a 2026-10-29
HELP WEAPON MASTERY (or HELP MASTERY) now explains a warrior's and a
thief's weapon mastery: how much it adds to each blow, and why it is
greater in your own class's guild.

@ 20261028b 2026-10-28
A target that only starts the word SELF (KILL S, LOOK SE) now means
whoever in the room it names, not you; SELF in full still means you.
AQUEST away from a questmaster says where Questor Thews is. In Hyrule's
Hall of Grumbling, LOOK STONES and LOOK SHUTTER now say what holds the
north passage.

@ 20261028a 2026-10-28
HELP finds a page from a shortened name of more than one word: HELP
DIVINE INTER finds DIVINE INTERVENTION, HELP STONE SK finds STONE SKIN.
HELP TRANSPORTATION now finds the transport spell group.

@ 20261027n 2026-10-27 staff
GRANTPSI <name> now waits for the awakening check (the first level they
gain from 18 to 21; after a remort if they are past it). GRANTPSI <name>
LEVEL gives psionics on their next level, NOW at once, online or not.
None of them tells the player; staff get a WIZINFO naming the powers
the moment they are actually given.

@ 20261027m 2026-10-27
PRAY from a safe room, such as the altar of the Temple, and you come back
from the Oracle with no daze at all. RECALL that misses no longer says
the gods are listening to somebody else.

@ 20261027l 2026-10-27
Hermie no longer appears at the altar on her own after the game restarts.
She comes when the immortals call her; WHERE HERMIE finds her when she is
about.

@ 20261027k 2026-10-27
The Games Room on the campus has one arcade cabinet to Hyrule now, not
two: both led to the same place. ENTER CABINET as before.

@ 20261027j 2026-10-27
LOOK at The Triforce now draws it. The Master Sword and the steel shield
no longer answer to the word TRIFORCE, so LOOK TRIFORCE and WEAR TRIFORCE
always mean the Triforce.

@ 20261027i 2026-10-27
Hyrule, Level 7: the Hall of Grumbling now tells you how to get past its
hungry Goriya. LOOK at the bowl, the bones, the scratches or the Goriya,
or LOOK BAIT to learn where enemy bait is sold. Bring bait and type FEED
GORIYA. The bait itself says the same.

@ 20261027h 2026-10-27
The help has been checked against the game and corrected: the psionic
powers, the thief and warrior skills, colour spray, the quest potions,
Farslay and many more now say what they really do. RULES, NEWS and STORY
show their pages again, and HELP GROUP <name> lists a spell group even
where a command shares its name (HELP GROUP WEATHER).

@ 20261027g 2026-10-27
Monsters that cast flamestrike or lightning bolt hit as hard as they did
before today's balance change. Only players' spells grow with their
level; a priest of the temple no longer burns for five times its level.

@ 20261027f 2026-10-27
Coming back from the Oracle no longer looks like the game froze. For a
minute after an audience your mind needs to recover: every command but
QUIT is answered at once with how long is left, and you are told when
your head clears. Before, the first command you typed simply sat there
for a minute.

@ 20261027e 2026-10-27
Crafting: BREW, CONCOCT and SCRIBE PREVIEW show for free what the
ingredients you carry would make, its spells, your chance and what a
failure costs. The ironbound scroll's major globe now forms -- it is
giant strength, bless and the globe. A scroll can no longer be read at
itself, and one that works on an object wants an object you carry. A
fatal cauldron blast uses up its ingredients instead of leaving them in
your corpse. Crafted things answer to the spell they are known for
(RECITE GLOBE), and say what they are when they lie on the ground.

@ 20261027d 2026-10-27
GAINLIST PREVIEW shows second and third attack as the chances they are,
with the swings a round you can expect at each level and what dual
wield adds -- not as sure extra blows.

@ 20261027c 2026-10-27
A death and a resurrection now reach your file before anything else
happens to your belongings: a corpse cannot be looted until its death
is saved (a moment), and a crash at the wrong second can no longer
leave your gear both on you and in your corpse.

@ 20261027b 2026-10-27
Iron skin now tells you which weapons it has made you immune to --
blunt, piercing or slashing -- and AFFECTS shows "grants immunity to
blunt" instead of "modifies (unknown)".

@ 20261027a 2026-10-27
Balance: warriors, thieves, mages and clerics hit much harder, to stand
beside monks and necromancers. Warriors and thieves gain weapon mastery:
their weapon blows grow with every level, most of all in their own
class's guild (HELP WARRIOR, HELP THIEF). Every cleric's flamestrike and
every mage's lightning bolt now grow a die each level (HELP FIRE SPELLS,
HELP ELECTRIC SPELLS). Nothing was made weaker.

@ 20261026n 2026-10-26
Balance: HEAL now grows with the caster's level -- still 100 at 25, then
two more a level, 150 at 50 and 168 at 59 (HELP HEALSPELL). A smite no
longer snaps your weapon outright: now and then it wears it down, and only
a weapon worn to nothing breaks (HELP SMITE). And a necromancer's servant
is built from the necromancer's own hit points, not from what a spell
like TITANIC lends them for a while.

@ 20261026m 2026-10-26
GAINLIST PREVIEW <class> <guild> shows any class and guild before you
choose: everything it is given and can GAIN, at the level each opens,
the trains it costs, its blows a round, and what a guild outside your
class's own adds and gives up. GAINLIST also stopped listing cause
serious and cause critical for builds that can never learn them.

@ 20261026k 2026-10-26
Combat fixes: backstab and smite now hit more surely the better you know
them (a mastered backstab used to miss more than a half-learned one);
psionic armor and psychic shield now take a quarter off mental damage,
as they always claimed to; a warrior's destruction no longer costs the
third attack when it fails; crane dance strikes on one smooth scale
instead of dropping suddenly against tougher foes; and a necromancer's
servants share one budget (HELP CREATE SKELETON), whatever order they
are raised in.

@ 20261026j 2026-10-26 staff
PRESTORE can bring back a deleted character from a snapshot taken
before the deletion, with the same identity, unless the name has
passed to someone else since. Notices about a wizinvis immortal now
stay at their wizinvis level.

@ 20261026i 2026-10-26
ACCEPTing a resurrection takes what is left in your corpse only once
your character is safely saved. If the save fails you are told,
everything stays in the corpse, and you can ACCEPT again.

@ 20261026h 2026-10-26
The Oracle can now tell you where your own corpse lies and how much is
still in it, and answers a question about one gear slot (arms, boots, a
ring) with the item itself. HELP FATALITY gives the actual odds.

@ 20261026g 2026-10-26
HELP DEATHTRAP explains death traps: what happens when you step into one,
how long you have, and what will never carry you into one.

@ 20261026f 2026-10-26
A player whose connection stalls no longer freezes the game for everyone
else for up to half a minute when the game lets them go.

@ 20261026e 2026-10-26
Walking a long corridor a step at a time -- a client's walker sending
"east" thirty times -- no longer trips the spam guard and throws you out
mid-quest. Any other command typed twenty-five times running still does.
HELP DAILY now finds the daily quests.

@ 20261026d 2026-10-26
A bomb Level 2's Dodongo swallows now hurts it: the blast inside takes
half its health, as the old man says. Its hide is proof against fire, and
the swallowed bomb was being turned aside by it.

@ 20261026c 2026-10-26
Some of Hyrule's dungeon rooms are as the old game built them: darknuts
where zols stood, three key doors that were missing, one that was locked
and should not be, and two passages in Death Mountain that were always
walls.

@ 20261026b 2026-10-26
Hyrule's White Sword can be wielded from level 10, not 30, so the hero
with the five hearts its old man asks for can use it when it is given.
One already held keeps the level it was made at.

@ 20261026a 2026-10-26
Some of Hyrule's keys, maps and compasses, and both boomerangs, now appear
only when the last enemy in their room falls, as in the old game -- you
will hear a chime. Patra has the map. Bubbles and blade traps never need
to die for it. Seven keys the old game had and ours did not are back.

@ 20261025o 2026-10-25
Hyrule's tools lie where the old game kept them. The bow is in Level 1's
cellar, the raft in Level 3's, the stepladder in Level 4's, the Recorder
in Level 5's, the Red Candle in Level 7's and the Magical Key in Level 8's
(PUSH BLOCK, then DOWN); the boomerangs lie with the goriyas of Levels 1
and 2. The guardians' chests hold their Triforce pieces. Digdogger cannot
be hurt until the Recorder is played at it. Anything you already carry is
yours to keep.

@ 20261025n 2026-10-25
Hyrule's enemies keep the old game's rules. Only an arrow finishes Gohma:
SHOOT her with the bow, not a sword swung while holding one. An arrow
bursts a pols voice and a boomerang drops a keese or a gel every time. A
patra's great eye is out of reach until its ring of eight eyes is cut
down. Bubbles and blade traps cannot be harmed -- go round them -- and no
longer keep a shutter shut. Every Dodongo swallows a bomb for half its
health. A like like eats only the Magical Shield. The Blue Candle flares
once a room; the Red at will. Manhandla's heads matter: fewer, harder
fireballs as they fall. The money game wants 40 gold, the worst sign.

@ 20261025m 2026-10-25
Hyrule's mazes are where the old game keeps them. The Lost Woods are in the
far west, between the Old Forest Clearing and the Western Meadow Edge:
north, west, south, west to get through, and east always gets you out. The
Lost Hills guard the Lizard's Gate: north four times, not five, and west
always gets you out. Death Mountain's stone stairs no longer ask for the
stepladder, and the Western Crags no longer ask for the raft.

@ 20261025l 2026-10-25
SHOVE takes a direction the way moving does: SHOVE GUARD SO works, not
only S or SOUTH. A stone skin pill or potion now says it never takes on a
monk or a necromancer, instead of "Spell failed." And Level 7's Hidden
Cistern answers LOOK CISTERN, NOSE, TIP and MOSS.

@ 20261025k 2026-10-25
SHOVE no longer moves Hyrule's enemies and guardians: a dungeon's shutters
open for foes beaten, not foes pushed into the next room. Each shove also
takes a moment now, like any other skill. See HELP SHOVE.

@ 20261025j 2026-10-25
FISTS OF FURY at a named foe now starts the fight and strikes. Out of a
fight it used to cost the mana and moves and land nothing; only plain
FISTS in a fight already going worked.

@ 20261025h 2026-10-25
Members of the cleric guild, of any class, can learn RESURRECTION (Qualo
the healer trains it). Cast over a fallen player's corpse, it asks them:
ACCEPT brings them back to the body at one hit point with everything it
held, DECLINE lets the call fade. See HELP RESURRECTION.

@ 20261025i 2026-10-25
TITANIC and EMPOWER, the bundles Hermie gives free, can now be made to
carry: there is a concoction and an ink for each, waiting to be found.
SCRIBE also tells you what you wrote.

@ 20261025e 2026-10-25
175 new achievements, 378 in all. Chase treasure goblins and the black
dragon, buy from Vesh, rescue and heal your group, master your skills,
explore every corner, walk Hyrule's secrets and win its Fair Fights. Long
lists come in parts now: ACHIEVEMENTS ALL 2 is the second. See HELP
ACHIEVEMENTS.

@ 20261025f 2026-10-25
Every achievement point is also a mark to spend. REDEEM shows what marks
buy: a trophy for an achievement, a new name for your weapon, more stash
room, or your recall point moved early. Spending never lowers your points.

@ 20261025g 2026-10-25
BREW, CONCOCT and SCRIBE are fairer: a combination that makes nothing, or
an herb no brew uses, costs nothing; each real attempt takes a few seconds;
what you make is your level. There are thirteen new potions and scrolls to
discover, and spell components spawn again where they had stopped.

@ 20261025d 2026-10-25
TELEKINESIS looks before it reaches. When nothing by that name lies
anywhere it can reach -- a corpse that has rotted away, say -- or the only
match is gear TK can never fetch, it tells you so and costs nothing,
instead of "You lost your concentration." HELP TK says what it can and
cannot fetch, and that it starts at 1% until practised with Salir.

@ 20261025a 2026-10-25
WALKTO QUEST walks anyone on a quest to the entrance of the area the
quest master named; finding the quarry there is still yours. It used to
answer that it was for immortals.

@ 20261025b 2026-10-25
Hermie lifts every curse at once when you say UNCURSE, instead of one
item each time you ask. "Your the cloak glows blue" reads properly now.

@ 20261025c 2026-10-25
HELP CRANE, FISTS, IRON, STEEL and ROLL described fighting stances that
do not exist. They now show the monk skills those commands really are
(crane dance, fists of fury, iron skin, steel fist) and the dice roller.
HELP PARAGON and the other alignment tiers find HELP ALIGNMENT.

@ 20261024e 2026-10-24
CONSIDER sizes up the fight itself now: how your level and hit points
compare, about how many rounds each of you would need to bring the
other down, one verdict, and anything that changes the odds (sanctuary,
speed, a monster that attacks on sight). It no longer tells you a foe is
easy and deadly in the same breath. See HELP CONSIDER.

@ 20261024d 2026-10-24
A word that starts your own name now finds the monster first: KILL TR
among trolls attacks a troll instead of telling you to MURDER a player.
SELF still means you. CONSIDER also works in the Temple now.

@ 20261024a 2026-10-24
GROUP names everyone in your group, even one you cannot see: a member
hidden by stealth or invisibility no longer shows as "Someone".

@ 20261024b 2026-10-24
The Mudlet quest strip is clickable again (package 1.5.10): it walks you
to the area your quest target was last seen in, as WALK QUEST does.

@ 20261024c 2026-10-24 staff
A character restored to a "before death" snapshot no longer logs in dead.
Anyone read from a file dying stands up at one hit point in the Temple.

@ 20261023m 2026-10-23
The Mudlet package (1.5.9) removes Mudlet's generic mapper if your profile
has it, once, and tells you. It was what printed "Prompt not
auto-detected" at login; this package draws your map from the game, and
your map is kept.

@ 20261023l 2026-10-23
HEAL UNCURSE at Hermie now says why it cannot reach your gear: while
NOSUMMON is on, cursed gear is closed to remove curse. Type NOSUMMON to
open it. With nothing cursed she says so, instead of calling you immune.

@ 20261023k 2026-10-23
Madame Hexley and Tinsel no longer list the same item ten times: each
holiday item shows once, and they never run out.

@ 20261023i 2026-10-23
Your corpse now lasts a week instead of minutes, and a reboot no longer
takes it: it comes back where you fell with exactly what was still in it.
If it rots or is lost with things inside, the staff can give those back.
The game also keeps a copy of you before every death and remort and after
every level and quest, so the staff can give back what a death or a bug
cost you.

@ 20261023j 2026-10-23 staff
PRESTORE lists how long ago each copy was taken, filters by kind (DEATHS,
REMORTS, LEVELS, QUESTS, RESTORES, MILESTONES, ALL -- a page at a time),
and has new forms: <stamp> SHOW lists worn, carried and stashed items;
<stamp> GEAR puts what they wore and carried into their inventory and
changes nothing else; CORPSES and CORPSE <id> SHOW|GEAR give back what a
lost corpse held. A death by a mobile also keeps a copy from before its
experience penalty. A restore can be asked for through git
(area/restores.dat) and never runs twice. Every restore takes its undo
copy first and changes nothing if it cannot, and a full restore keeps
the player's current password, rank and one-time claims. HELP PRESTORE,
wiki/player-backups.md.

@ 20261023g 2026-10-23
Disasters are fairer. Floods, lightning, earthquakes, tornadoes, sand
storms, brush fires and tidal waves now warn the area a few seconds
before they strike, never kill you, and spare the Temple, the altar,
safe rooms and anybody below level 10. An earthquake throws you down
for a moment instead of stunning you, a sand storm really does blind
you, and a lightning storm comes with lightning. HELP DISASTERS.

@ 20261023f 2026-10-23
The Great Black Dragon hunts again. Now and then it swoops down on
somebody standing outdoors, carries them off to another part of the
area and lands beside them. It will not attack: KILL DRAGON for its
hoard -- coin and always a good piece of gear for your level -- or walk
away and it leaves. HELP 'BLACK DRAGON'.

@ 20261023h 2026-10-23 staff
DISASTER lists areas suffering a disaster and where the dragon waits;
DISASTER <kind> strikes your area (after the usual warning), DISASTER
STOP ends it, and DISASTER DRAGON <player> sends the dragon for them.
HELP DISASTER.

@ 20261023e 2026-10-23
Coloured custom prompts now show their colours instead of the colour tags,
and stay plain with COLOR OFF. The browser client keeps terminal control
codes out of your transcript and starts with clean colours when reconnecting.
Mudlet 1.5.8 automatically updates the chat pane for the new COLOR choices.

@ 20261023d 2026-10-23
Twenty-four new colours for COLOR: orange, amber, gold, lime, mint,
teal, turquoise, sky, navy, indigo, purple, violet, lavender, pink, rose,
crimson, maroon, coral, salmon, peach, tan, olive, silver and charcoal.
COLOR LIST shows all forty in their own colours; pick one by name, as in
COLOR GOSSIPS ORANGE. They need a client with 256 colours -- Mudlet and
the web client both have them. The web client also draws background
colours and reverse text properly now, and Mudlet's chat window no
longer shows colour codes as letters (the package updates itself).

@ 20261023c 2026-10-23
Colour fixes:
- COLOR OFF now stays off when you log back in.
- AREAS shows each area's level range whole, as [30 50], instead of
  half of it.
- Colour typed into a channel or SAY shows as colour to everyone who
  hears it, not as letters and numbers.
- A coloured title no longer tints the rest of the line, and a long one
  is never cut in the middle of a colour.
- Setting a colour to plain no longer leaves the colour before it running.

@ 20261023b 2026-10-23 staff
What a wizinvis or unseen immortal does TO a player names them "an
immortal": "An immortal pokes you", "An immortal tells you ...", a
channel line, a spell aimed at them. Anything the room would see --
arriving, leaving, a poof, a SAY -- still shows nothing at all.
CHANGES shows entries like this one, marked (staff only), to staff
alone.

@ 20261023a 2026-10-23
- Hermie always answers when you ask her by HEAL or BUFF: a word she does
  not know gets her list instead of silence.
- OPEN, CLOSE, LOCK and UNLOCK on an exit with no door now say there is
  no door that way, instead of "You can't do that."

@ 20261022g 2026-10-22
- The underbrush east of the Coven's logging trail is no longer locked:
  open it and the witches beyond are yours to hunt, no sickle needed.
- The dagger-wielding imps of the Upper Argo no longer attack on sight.

@ 20261022f 2026-10-22
- WIMPY now works when you attack and then just watch the fight: your
  attack's moment of lag wears off during the fight, so you flee at your
  wimpy as you should.  It used to wait for you to type something.
- A vampiric weapon heals you only from blows that actually hurt: a
  parried, dodged or blocked blow, or one the foe is immune to, feeds you
  nothing.
- Gear worn all the way down to nothing breaks and falls into your pack,
  as it does a point later; take it to a smith.

@ 20261022e 2026-10-22
Fixes and conveniences:
- BOMB uses a bomb you carry, in any bag, and only once. Bombs in your
  stash still count against your bomb bag, but you must take them out
  to use them -- they no longer go off from the stash.
- REPAIR now puts armour back exactly as it was before heat, acid or a
  dented shield wore it down, even pieces that were rolled better than
  usual. Damage from before today repairs as it always did.
- Riding into a trapped room sets the trap off once, not twice.
- Heat metal no longer says it had no effect when it burned.
- REPAIR QUOTE <item> or REPAIR QUOTE ALL: the price and what comes back,
  from anywhere, without paying.
- DEVOTE PREVIEW: where each devotion would leave you, what it costs, and
  what worn gear would fall off, from anywhere and for nothing.
- AQUEST INFO and AQUEST DAILY say when your next quest or daily may be
  taken and why not yet, and what giving up the current one would cost.

@ 20261022d 2026-10-22
More fixes from the same audit:
- A failed ENCHANT ARMOR that leaves a piece "glowing blue, then fading"
  now leaves it in your pack, damaged. It used to vanish.
- STASH refuses a bag holding something that will rot, which went in and
  quietly crumbled away there.
- A line too long to send no longer swallows the commands typed after it.
- Notes are private, like tells: their subject and text are no longer
  written to the game's activity logs.

@ 20261022c 2026-10-22
A round of fixes from a code audit:
- Haggling for a part-used wand or staff takes money off its real price;
  it can no longer come out free.
- REPAIR no longer charges to "repair" armour that was never damaged.
- REMORT puts back on only what your new body can wear: a weapon now too
  heavy, or an off-hand weapon without dual wield, goes in your pack.
- SECONDARY refuses a weapon whose own bonuses are over +5, or one the
  enchant spells have worked on, as it always meant to.
- Heat no longer erases an item's own countdown.
- LOOK IN a portal no longer counts as visiting the room beyond.
- CLIMB, CRAWL and JUMP respect private, newbie and hero rooms and cannot
  carry you out of a fight; CRAWL and JUMP need you standing.
- Meteor swarm strikes each target up to four times again.
- Divine protection strikes back with an ordinary blow.
- At login, gear you could not wear now (a second Blue Ring, something
  above your level) is put in your pack.
- Two people can no longer create the same new name at the same moment.

A remort that keeps a two-handed weapon no longer gets a school shield
strapped on beside it, and neither does OUTFIT: you have no hand for one,
as WEAR has always said. The shield stays in your pack.

@ 20261022a 2026-10-22
HELP HEROQUEST no longer describes a hero quest that does not exist: those
commands are long gone, and heroes quest with AQUEST like everyone else.
When a buff that raised your hit points, mana or moves wears off, what it
added now goes with it at once, instead of lingering until the next tick.

@ 20261021l 2026-10-21
A remort no longer puts on a broken starter piece from your pack: it
stays in the pack and you get a fresh one. A monk who remorts while
carrying a weapon now starts with hand to hand trained, as every monk
should.

@ 20261021k 2026-10-21
Remort keeps your pet: if it was beside you, it comes to the Temple with
you. A remort with old school gear in your pack now gets its starting
kit -- OUTFIT puts on a matching piece you carry or makes a new one, for
each empty slot. Practices and trains above 30,000 are no longer cut at a
remort. Arrows shot into the next room now respect immunities and
sanctuary. The web client never shows an unsent password if the
connection drops.

@ 20261021j 2026-10-21
Fixes from a code review: hostile spells are refused in the Temple and
safe rooms, as attacks are; heat metal and acid breath no longer leave you
better armoured after the piece comes off; a trap that kills you on your
way out ends the move; HISTORY TELL shows tells only; and REPAIR mends a
dented shield. Repair no longer changes what an item sells for. The web
client sends a line with semicolons as you typed it, so "\;" stays text
and an ALIAS keeps its whole body. Routes through a locked door now say
which key, or PASS DOOR, they need.

@ 20261021i 2026-10-21
BUG, TYPO and IDEA now keep the room you are in and your last few
commands with the report, so type them right where something went wrong.
The game also records what it answers your commands (never tells,
replies, group tells or passwords) to help find bugs. See HELP BUG.

@ 20261021h 2026-10-21
Haggling still raises what a shopkeeper pays you, but never above what the
thing is worth. REPAIR ALL works in the dark, USE BOMB BAG finds a bag you
are holding, and the pit healer will not take your money for an uncurse
while NOSUMMON closes your gear to it -- it tells you instead.

@ 20261021g 2026-10-21
Alignment is rebuilt. It has seven tiers now -- Paragon, Virtuous and Kind
of the light, Balanced, and Ruthless, Vile and Fiend of the dark -- and
each gives something: the light heals faster and strikes harder with holy
power, the dark drains life with its blows, the balanced shrug off holy
and negative damage. You are what you slay: the evil move you toward the
light, the good toward the dark, the neutral not at all. Slaying the other
side pays more experience, shopkeepers favour their own side, and DEVOTE
at the Temple steers you on purpose. Type ALIGNMENT to see where you stand;
the Mudlet package (1.5.7) shows your tier beside your class.

@ 20261021f 2026-10-21
Alignment is no longer stuck at -1000 or 1000: slaying the other side
always moves you back. See the alignment entry above, and HELP ALIGNMENT.

@ 20261021e 2026-10-21
REPAIR ALL mends everything you wear and carry that needs it, cheapest
first. The quest cooldown now runs while you are logged out. The pit
healer will not charge for an uncurse when nothing on you is cursed.
Messages that showed odd symbols where a dash belonged read properly now.

@ 20261021d 2026-10-21
The treasure goblin can no longer be held at all: stuns, sleep, bash,
trip and confusion are shaken off at once, and every blow that lands
sends him running. Keep chasing!

@ 20261021c 2026-10-21
If you are not a mage and found mage spells in your skill list, they came
from the same mistake: they are taken back when you next log in, and any
practice sessions you spent on them are returned to you.

@ 20261021b 2026-10-21
New characters now start with their own class's skills and spells only.
A mistake had been giving every new character the mage's starting spells
as well.

@ 20261020l 2026-10-20
Fixes: bash, trip and stunning blow now hold the treasure goblin, and
nobody can FOLLOW him or the black market dealer. Abandoning a daily
quest means ten minutes before the next. HIDE says plainly when you are
fighting. PRACTICE always teaches at least a point a session. The
dealer's goods can be seen in the dark, and he no longer takes over
other shops. Mudlet shows DAILY on the quest bar.

@ 20261020k 2026-10-20
Rested experience: quit in a safe or healing room, the Temple, the altar
or your recall point, and each hour away banks bonus experience -- kills
pay double until it is spent. RESTED shows it. Daily quests: AQUEST DAILY
REQUEST, three a day, pays daily points; keep a daily streak going and
they pay more. A month of every daily buys a train with AQUEST DAILY BUY.
New achievements for both. WALKTO QUEST is now for immortals only.
HELP RESTED, HELP AQUEST.

@ 20261020j 2026-10-20
USE <item> now does the obvious thing with whatever you hold: quaff,
recite, eat, drink, zap, play or wear it. A command the game does not
know suggests the one you probably meant. Quests are drawn from the
whole world around your level again instead of the same few areas, and
pay coin worth something at your level. Alignment no longer slips past
-1000 or 1000. HELP USE.

@ 20261020i 2026-10-20
A treasure goblin is loose somewhere in the world -- there is always one.
He never fights back: hit him and he spills coin and runs, and you will
have to chase him a dozen rooms and more. Keep at him or he slips away
through a portal. Stuns hold him. Run him down and his whole sack is
yours, coin and often gear for your level. HELP TREASURE GOBLIN.
The Oracle's sanctum is no place to sleep: she sends you out at once.

@ 20261020h 2026-10-20
Travellers whisper of Vesh the Smuggler, the black market, who sells
what cannot be had anywhere else -- five things at a time, one of each
to a customer. He is seldom in the world, never in one place for long,
and nobody can say where he is. HELP BLACK MARKET.

@ 20261020g 2026-10-20
Salir, and every trainer, now says when you can train a skill you hold
but are too low for, instead of "You can't practice that." A remort
no longer takes away a shadowmeld an immortal gave you. HELP PSIONICS
lists the four disciplines and what each remort gives.

@ 20261020f 2026-10-20
RECALL on the spot you would recall to now says so and names it,
instead of a bare "You are already there."

@ 20261020e 2026-10-20
TRACK no longer points a random way when you miss: it says the trail
was lost, and a good roll says how far off your quarry is. HIDE tells
you whether it worked. PRACTICE <skill> 5, or MAX, spends that many
sessions at once. The temple healer's REFRESH fills your legs in one
go, at the same price a casting. HELP HERO, EXCHANGE, HITROLL, DESPAIR
and every psionic power answer at any level, and a mistyped HELP
suggests what you meant.

@ 20261020d 2026-10-20
The Hallows End decorations answer LOOK: the pumpkins, the scarecrows,
the coffins and the knocking, forty-odd things in all. CHAT is GOSSIP
for those who kept typing it. HELP QUEST, QUESTING, THEWS, HERMIE,
ACCOUNT and FOURTH ATTACK answer now, and a shopkeeper who cannot see
you says why.

@ 20261020c 2026-10-20
Dresden has dressed properly for Hallows End: every decorated street,
hall and shopkeeper has a look of its own this year, and the Temple of
Devota is the acolytes' haunted house, for the orphanage. Go and look.

@ 20261020b 2026-10-20
The Headless Horseman waits in Oak Tree Square now instead of riding off
around Dresden, and he attacks nobody who does not attack him; Father
Winter will do the same at Winter Veil. LOOK at either and you are told
what he drops and how often.

@ 20261020a 2026-10-20 staff
A wizinvis immortal leaves no trace with players below the level: no
"An Immortal appears in the room" when they recall, no arrivals or
departures, and their SAY and socials are not shown. Somebody unseen is
"someone"; an unseen immortal who does something to a player -- a poke,
a tell, a spell -- is "an immortal" to them.

@ 20261019b 2026-10-19
Hallows End is on until the first of November: Dresden, Limbo and Mud
School take their Halloween dress at the next reboot, with everything
the ordinary world has in them this time -- the Quest Master, Hermie,
the Oracle and the shops' real prices included.

@ 20261019a 2026-10-19
HELP ALIGNMENT explains what your alignment does and what moves it, HELP
CLASS lists the six classes and where each is described, and HELP
INTEREST reaches the bank's terms.

@ 20261017a 2026-10-17
HELP answers more of what new players ask: STRENGTH, DEXTERITY and the
other attributes by name, STATS, DEATH and CORPSE, CASTLES, and TRAITOR.

@ 20261013a 2026-10-13
PICK now tells you at once when a lock cannot be picked at all, instead
of answering "You failed" as if you had missed the roll; a missed roll
is a fumble, told a different way each time, and means the lock can open
so trying again is worth it. STEAL fumbles the same way instead of
saying "Oops", a RECALL the gods do not answer says so, and BACKSTAB on
a wounded target tells you they are hurt and suspicious rather than
"You failed". STEAL from somebody far above your level says they are
too wary for you, since that can never work.

@ 20261010a 2026-10-10
Dying no longer empties your stash. HISTORY with nothing to show now
says nothing has been said on any channel.

@ 20261008b 2026-10-08
In Mud School, ISSUE, REISSUE and SUBISSUE now hand out your sub issue
gear, just as OUTFIT does, and HELP SUBISSUE finds it.

@ 20261008a 2026-10-08
WALKTO QUEST walks you to where the quest master sent you, and the quest
master now only sends you somewhere you can walk to -- no more quests to
rooms nobody can reach. AFFECTS works as well as AFFECT, and the browser
client's Affects button works again. On the website, the Gear Finder now
offers a thief a second weapon for the off hand (SECONDARY) from level
17, when dual wield is learned.

@ 20261005d 2026-10-05
BUY and TRAIN take a count: BUY 10 FLY buys ten potions, TRAIN HP 10 uses
ten sessions. Each stops at the first one you cannot afford, carry or
train, and tells you how many it managed. HELP now answers every spell
group by name -- HELP NECRO MALADICTIONS lists what is in it and what it
costs you -- and HELP DOOR BASH finds DOORBASH.

@ 20261005c 2026-10-05
Saying something with a $ in it now shows you exactly what you said, as
everyone else already saw it, and ordering a pet to do something with a $
in it no longer garbles the order it hears. The WHOOSH social says
*whooshes* to its target properly.

@ 20261005a 2026-10-05
A chest you have just unlocked and opened no longer slams shut and locks
itself before you can take what is inside, and a locked box in your pack no
longer locks itself in your hands. Chests left lying in empty rooms still
lock themselves again for the next visitor.

@ 20261005b 2026-10-05
Reconnecting straight after you quit no longer drops you at the password
prompt without a word: a quit still waiting out lag used to hang up on the
new login as well.

@ 20261004t 2026-10-04
Hyrule's dungeon enemies were fought one by one against the world's own
mobiles of the same levels. Levels 1 to 5, 8 and 9 already matched the
world. Level 6's enemies ran a little tough and have fewer hit points now;
Level 7's ran soft and have more. Ganon was played against groups: a pair
buffed by Hermie can beat him, a lone character still cannot.

@ 20261004s 2026-10-04
Hyrule's guardians were played through in the real game and retuned. Each
is a hard fight for its dungeon's levels: an ordinary character at the top
of the band loses alone, but buffed by Hermie first (BUFF EMPOWER, TITANIC,
DEFENSE and COMBAT) can win, usually with little health to spare. Ganon
still wants a buffed group. Manhandla no longer shrugs off clubs and maces,
nor Gohma swords; Gohma has lost her sanctuary, but only an arrow finishes
her, so carry the bow.

@ 20261004a 2026-10-04
GAINLIST now shows every skill and spell your class and guild can learn,
ticked (+) when you have it and crossed (X) when you do not, with what to
GAIN for it, which trainer sells it, where they stand and the WALKTO that
takes you there. ABILITIES is the same command, and GAINLIST TRAINERS is
the old list of what each trainer sells.

@ 20261004b 2026-10-04
The Oracle knows what you are missing. PRAY and ask her what skills or
spells you have not learned, and she answers from the game itself, with
the trainer and the way to them.

@ 20261004c 2026-10-04
Gate, earth travel and portal reach the first creature or person of that
name you could actually get to: anyone not in a no-recall room or a jail,
not immortal, and no more than four levels above you. 2.kitten is the
second such kitten. Astral walk has no level limit and can leave a no-
recall room, but never enter one.

@ 20261004d 2026-10-04
Hyrule can be done in order now. Levels 1 and 2 stood behind river
crossings that needed the raft, which is Level 3's treasure, and Level 4's
island behind a ladder that is Level 4's own. There are stepping stones, a
ferry and a plank bridge there now. Reported by Alaric.

@ 20261004e 2026-10-04
Nothing in Hyrule attacks first any more, and its creatures are as tough
as the rest of the world's at the same level - no tougher, no softer. The
land around each dungeon is graded for that dungeon, and HELP HYRULE lists
the character levels each dungeon is built for and where it is.

@ 20261004f 2026-10-04
Every Hyrule guardian can drop a piece for every armour slot, each the
best in the game for its dungeon's levels, for fighters and casters alike,
and three fall each kill. The guardians' weapons and Heart Guards are
stronger too.

@ 20261004g 2026-10-04
In Hyrule, enemies killed near a cracked wall sometimes leave a bomb, so
you are not sent back to a shop to get past a wall the dungeon put in
front of you.

@ 20261004h 2026-10-04
The Recorder: PLAY RECORDER (or BLOW RECORDER) out in Hyrule's open land
calls a whirlwind that carries you to any dungeon you have won and to the
one you are working on. PLAY RECORDER <level> picks one. Where a puzzle
wants the tune, the puzzle still gets it.

@ 20261004i 2026-10-04
Leave a Hyrule dungeon you have won by its returning light and an owl
lands to tell you where the next dungeon is and what opens it. The Oracle
knows every path in Hyrule too, and gives directions from wherever you
stand.

@ 20261004j 2026-10-04
A Hyrule treasure chest is never relocked while you are standing at it.

@ 20261004k 2026-10-04
Mudlet 1.5.5: Hyrule's dungeons are no longer on the starter map. Pick up
a dungeon's map and the whole dungeon is drawn on yours.

@ 20261004l 2026-10-04
Commands typed on one line with semicolons between them - n;n;e - run one
after another in any client, as they always did in the browser client.

@ 20261004m 2026-10-04
The quest master tells you your quest instead of announcing it to the
room.

@ 20261004n 2026-10-04
A remort keeps your unspent practices and trains, and your own flaming
aura never burns you.

@ 20261004o 2026-10-04
Spells your class can learn from another class's trainer are taught now,
and so is DESPAIR. MAJOR GLOBE, the travel spells, riding, MAZE and WALKTO
had fixes of their own.

@ 20261004p 2026-10-04
The slot machines pay back about 93 percent, and limited items you put in
your stash stay yours.

@ 20261004q 2026-10-04
Mud School's north cage now warns you plainly: its monster attacks the
moment you walk in, so go in rested and FLEE if it turns against you.

@ 20261004r 2026-10-04
The play page has a link to the gear finder: the best gear for your class
and level, and where it drops.

@ 20261003a 2026-10-03
Psionic powers start at 1% until you practise them with Salir, including
powers handed back after a remort.

@ 20261003b 2026-10-03
Nobody can remort or level past the level cap, and every necromancer spell
now has a trainer. SCRIBE is taught by Dawn for every class.

@ 20261003c 2026-10-03
WALKTO <place> walks you to any area, guild hall, guildmaster or trainer
from wherever you stand, a step at a time. Type anything to stop. See HELP
WALKTO.

@ 20261003d 2026-10-03
The Oracle knows every guild hall, guildmaster and trainer, and the way to
each.

@ 20261003e 2026-10-03
Hyrule's nine dungeons are done in order: each guardian drops a key to its
treasure chest, which holds a Triforce piece and the treasure the next
dungeon needs. COMBINE TRIFORCE joins all nine. Ganon guards the Master
Sword and is a fight for a group. Dungeon maps and compasses show you the
way. See HELP HYRULE.

@ 20261003f 2026-10-03
Hyrule prices everything in ordinary gold.

@ 20261003g 2026-10-03
Stealth and shadowmeld cannot be seen through without holylight - there is
no roll any more, so you no longer flicker in and out of sight.

@ 20261003h 2026-10-03
REPAIR costs what your kills can pay for.

@ 20261003i 2026-10-03
Characters can have more than 32,767 hit points.

@ 20261003j 2026-10-03
Heroes never get too full to eat, and nobody sees 'No help on that word'
at login. Reported by Alaric.

@ 20261003k 2026-10-03
Every guild has infravision, titles stay set, and an ALIAS can run several
commands separated by semicolons.

@ 20261003l 2026-10-03
An item the game retires is swapped for its replacement at your next login
instead of vanishing.

@ 20261003m 2026-10-03
Mudlet 1.5.2 to 1.5.4: health, mana, endurance and experience are back
across the top, a failing part no longer hides the interface, death traps
are off the map, and travel routes load by default.

@ 20261002a 2026-10-02
COMPARE is rebuilt around how hard you hit, and COMPARE UPGRADES lists the
best pieces you could be wearing. The website's gear finder follows the
same rules.

@ 20261002b 2026-10-02
PRAY takes you to the Oracle's sanctum and back.

@ 20261002c 2026-10-02
Old bug and typo reports that were still true have been fixed, and the
disarm message has lost its stray space.

@ 20261001a 2026-10-01
The Oracle: PRAY to ask a seer about the game - gear, places, levelling,
how things work. See HELP ORACLE.

@ 20261001b 2026-10-01
A remort keeps every piece of your gear, bagging what your new level
cannot wear, and REPLAY is another name for HISTORY.

@ 20261001c 2026-10-01
SWEDISH works again.  The command set a flag but nothing read it: the
speech filter that garbles a swedished (or drunk) player's SAY and
channel text had been dropped in a refactor and left only as an
uncompiled file.  It is compiled and wired back into SAY and the
channels.  Drunk slurring returns with it.

@ 20261001d 2026-10-01
Mudlet 1.5.0 adds a combat-awareness set: a lag bar that shows when
you can act again, an enemy health gauge beside your own bars, a
Buffs tab with a countdown bar per spell, a Group tab showing each
party member's level and health, a low-health warning, and a Tells
tab that lights up on a new tell.  Update the package to get them.

@ 20261001e 2026-10-01
Mudlet: the quest strip now carries the target room, and clicking it
(or typing WALK QUEST) walks you straight there. The game sends the
room's vnum with the quest, so it is an exact path, not a guess by
name. Update the package to 1.4.0 to get it.

@ 20261001f 2026-10-01
The dashboard's gear finder names the best piece for each of your
eighteen slots for your class and level - both rings, both necks and
both wrists, two different items for each pair - then ranks every
item you could wear in each slot, Light included.  Plain
armour and shields were missing because their own armour class was
never counted, lights because they carry no wear flag, and an item
that made your saves worse was being ranked as if it made them
better.

@ 20261001g 2026-10-01 staff
Staff can eat anything again, to destroy an item they carry.  It
checked the character's level rather than their trust, so a builder
trusted to immortal rank was told the item was not edible.

@ 20261001h 2026-10-01
The training dummy can no longer be finished off.  A fatality
backstab killed it outright, because an instant kill never passed
the check that keeps it standing.  Backstab it and you get an
ordinary backstab, counted on the meter like any other blow; and
anything else that kills on the spot now finds it back on its post.

@ 20261001i 2026-10-01
AFFECT now lists psionic wards.  MINDBAR, PSIONIC ARMOR and PSYCHIC
SHIELD change no statistic - they are a named protection and a
duration - and the list was skipping exactly that shape, so the one
kind of effect you most want to confirm was the one you could not
see.  Reported by Alaric.  Psionics and skills are also no longer
announced as spells.

@ 20261001j 2026-10-01
Damage numbers now appear for every weapon.  Fifteen weapons in the
world carry no particular attack noun, and those went down a branch
of the combat message code that had never been given the bracketed
figure - so DAMAGENUMBERS worked for every weapon except the odd
ones, and for bare hands in some cases.  Reported by Alaric.

@ 20261001k 2026-10-01
A training yard, and a dummy in it that cannot be killed.  Go down
the staircase in the centre of the Oak Tree Square, then south -
WALK DUMMY in Mudlet takes you there - and KILL DUMMY.  HELP DUMMY
explains all of it.  The yard takes one fighter at a time, so nobody
else can walk into your run.

@ 20261001l 2026-10-01
Every run is the standard fight by default: twenty-five rounds, then a
bell, against a dummy at your own level that fights normally - it
dodges, parries, blocks and hits back.  Your best goes on a
leaderboard - DUMMY LEADERBOARD - and when a run ends you are told
whether it was a personal best, where you stand among everybody who
has run it, and how far the record is.  Post the best run anybody has
and you earn Top of the Board.

@ 20261001m 2026-10-01
Just attacking the dummy gives you the standard fight: when the yard
empties, it goes back to it, whatever the last fighter set.

@ 20261001n 2026-10-01
Only the standard fight is ranked.  DUMMY DEFENDS NO and DUMMY FIGHTS
NO take the dummy's own part out so you can measure your damage
alone, and DUMMY ROUNDS and DUMMY ENDLESS change the length - but
changing any setting at all means the run is not ranked, and the game
says so the moment you change it.

@ 20261001o 2026-10-01
Neither of you can die in the yard.  When a run ends you are put back
the way you were when it began - hit points, mana and moves - not
healed to full, so it is no place to recover.  Nothing is learned
there either: skills and spells do not improve in the yard.

@ 20261001p 2026-10-01
The report breaks the fight down attack by attack, both ways - every
spell you cast and every special attack on its own line, with its
damage, share, hit rate, average and best - alongside your totals,
damage per second, per swing and per round, and everything it did
to you.  Set the dummy up however the question needs: any level,
four shapes, nine damage types, a spell for it to cast, haste, a
different number of rounds, or DUMMY ENDLESS for a run with no
bell.

@ 20261001q 2026-10-01
A portal now refuses to take you into a private room that is full,
the way walking in always has.  It used to be the one way past.

@ 20261001r 2026-10-01
The quest master no longer asks you to kill the training dummy, which
cannot die.

@ 20261001s 2026-10-01
Mudlet shows your damage per round under the target: live during a
fight, then the last fight's once it ends.  Every fight counts, and
the game measures it, so it works with damage numbers off.  A new
line below the quest lists who else is online - only players you
could see, so nobody wizi, cloaked, stealthed or hidden.  Mudlet
offers the 1.3.0 package update automatically.

@ 20261001t 2026-10-01
City guards hunting a wanted player no longer follow them into the
Temple.  A hunter stops at the edge of a room mobiles may not enter,
as it always has at a safe one.

@ 20261001u 2026-10-01
If WALK DUMMY in Mudlet still heads somewhere else, TOCGUI ATLAS
reloads the map with the yard where it is now.

@ 20261001v 2026-10-01
The Mudlet chat window now shows each channel in the colour you
chose for it with COLOR, the same as the main window, and the quest
strip says where the quest master last saw your target.  Mudlet
offers the 1.3.1 package update automatically.

@ 20261001w 2026-10-01
The plaque in the Hall of Heroes lists every hero there has ever
been, and a new hero's name is on it the moment they are made - as
the room always said it would be.  LOOK PLAQUE, down from the
centre of the Oak Tree Square.

@ 20261001x 2026-10-01
POKE pokes again.  It was taken as the start of the longer command
POKER, so the social could never be used.  A word that is exactly a
social's name is now that social.

@ 20261001y 2026-10-01
COMBINE is back.  It switches your inventory between the combined
list - (3) a big pot pie - and the long one, and AUTOLIST shows which
you have.  It had been switched off while everything it controls
stayed on.  COMB is still the social, so type at least COMBI.

@ 20261001z 2026-10-01
Pyrotechnics now hits as hard as a fireball cast at your level.  It
used to scale with your current hit points, which made it about three
times its fellow psionics at level fifty and grew without limit with
every remort.  A failed attempt now costs its wait, as a failed cast
does, rather than letting you try again at once.  Heating the
victim's gear is still what it adds over a fireball.

@ 20260925a 2026-09-25
RECALL can be moved.  RECALL SET makes the room you are standing in your
recall point, RECALL DEFAULT puts it back to the Temple, and RECALL WHERE
tells you where it is.  Once every 30 minutes, and not mid-fight.

@ 20260925b 2026-09-25
The note board answers back.  NOTE REPLY <n> starts a note to
whoever wrote that one with the subject already set, NOTE FORWARD
<n> <player> passes one on, NOTE SEARCH finds a note by any word in
it, NOTE UNREAD shows only what is waiting and NOTE CATCHUP clears
the lot.  See HELP NOTE.

@ 20260925c 2026-09-25
HISTORY draws a line where you last logged out, so what was said
while you were away is easy to pick out.  Nothing is shown to you
automatically - you have to ask.

@ 20260925d 2026-09-25
HISTORY reads back what was said.  Type it on its own for the last
twenty lines across every channel you can hear, HISTORY 50 for more,
HISTORY GOSSIP for one channel, or HISTORY TELL for your own tells -
which stay private, and are kept per character.  It is held in memory
and is lost on a reboot, so it is a way to catch up rather than a
transcript.  See HELP HISTORY.

@ 20260925e 2026-09-25
You can set your recall point at the quest giver now.  A room was
being refused for being 'private', which is a count of who is standing
in it - the questmaster and you already made two - and that count
changes minute to minute, so a point set in a quiet moment would have
quietly reverted to the Temple later.  Only the permanent flags refuse
a recall point now.

@ 20260925f 2026-09-25
A mobile that lives in a room no longer fills it either.  The quest
giver's room holds two, and the questmaster was one of them.

@ 20260925g 2026-09-25 staff
An idle immortal no longer fills a one-person room.  Standing in the
quest room was enough to shut questing down for everybody else, which
is not what that flag is for - it exists to stop players walking in on
each other.  Staff can also walk into such a room now rather than
being turned away from it.

@ 20260925h 2026-09-25
STASH LINK has a help entry of its own at last: HELP STASHLINK covers
linking, denying, blocking and sharing in full, and HELP STASH lists
every subcommand rather than four of them.

@ 20260925i 2026-09-25
SHADOWMELD is a real skill now, and it is meant for two things: going
AFK without being killed for it, and laying in wait in a room somebody
has to walk through so that you strike first.

@ 20260925j 2026-09-25
The fourth remort teaches it at 50% and it improves from there with
use and with failure, like anything else.  A god can grant it to
anyone with SET SKILL.  No later remort takes it away, and once you
hold it you may practise it up.

@ 20260925k 2026-09-25
It behaves exactly like STEALTH against other players now rather than
like hide - the same roll against the same weather - so looking for
the hidden no longer finds you.  Holylight still does, and faerie fog
still reveals you.  VIS steps you out of it, WHO shows [SHADOW] beside
your name, WHERE leaves you off the list and DANGER SENSE counts you,
all exactly as they do for stealth.  Striking at somebody ends it,
whether you swing or cast.

@ 20260925l 2026-09-25
The recall that never fails has moved from the fourth remort down to
the third, to make room for shadowmeld.

@ 20260925m 2026-09-25
Remorting no longer cares which guilds you have belonged to, only
which classes you have lived as: mage, cleric, thief, warrior, monk,
necro.  Every life must be a class you have not played.  Join any
guild you like, as often as you like.

@ 20260925n 2026-09-25
The third remort now carries three gifts instead of one: twice the
carrying room, twice as long before the idle void, and a second psionic
power from each discipline.  Psionics STACK from now on -- a remort
remembers what it gave you and hands it back, so a later life never
costs you a power you already had, and the fifth remort gives you all
seventeen.

@ 20260925o 2026-09-25
Remorting no longer reads your class and guild history as one list.  It
used to, and because a guild is stored as its matching class, having
been in the mage guild barred you from ever living as a mage.  Worse, a
player who spent their choices badly could arrive at the fourth remort
with nothing legal left to pick, stuck at 57 with 59 out of reach.  The
two histories are separate now, 'none' is always a legal guild, and a
refusal lists everything still open to you.

@ 20260925p 2026-09-25
Two new gifts for remorting.  The remort taken at level 56 doubles
how long you may idle before the void takes you.  The one taken at
level 57 gives SHADOWMELD: draw the shadows around yourself and stay
in them until you move, sleeping if you like, with no creature in the
world able to see you.  It is meant for stepping away from the
keyboard.  See HELP SHADOWMELD.

@ 20260925q 2026-09-25
There is a stash at the altar now, one step west of recall.  STASH
PUT sets something aside from anywhere in the world; STASH GET takes
it back out, and that part only works at the altar.  Fifty things to
begin with, more for coin.  See HELP STASH.

@ 20260925r 2026-09-25
Hermie answers HEAL now, exactly like the healer at the pit and
with the same menu, except that everything she does is free.  She
no longer listens to what you say in the room.  She has ten more
spells than she did, six named groups, and REFRESH, HEAL and MANA
now fill the pool instead of handing out a slice at a time.  See
HELP BUFF.

@ 20260925s 2026-09-25
The healer at the pit tells you when a curse resists instead of
taking your gold in silence.

@ 20260925t 2026-09-25
The game says when something is waiting for you.  Unread notes are
announced at login instead of sitting unmentioned, and staff are told
how many bug, typo and idea reports have come in since they last
looked.  See HELP REPORTS.

@ 20260925u 2026-09-25 staff
Staff can now MIRROR a player's gear onto themselves to look at a
build from the inside, online or not, and INVULN stops anything hurting
them while they do it.  MIRROR RESTORE hands the borrowed kit back in a
pack and puts their own gear on again.

@ 20260925v 2026-09-25
Herbs and spell components actually appear now.  They had barely been
landing at all for years, and the scattering is deliberately sparse -
finding one should be a small event - and stops entirely when nobody is
logged in.

@ 20260925w 2026-09-25
Two monster wards that had never worked now do.  A bloody aura turns
magic aside; a dominion shield turns aside everything, and only goes up
when the creature is badly hurt.  Four end-game creatures use them: the
Lord General and the Fade in the Battleground, and Zoltan and the second
succubus in Valhalla.  See HELP DOMINION SHIELD.

@ 20260925x 2026-09-25
WORD OF RECALL is worth casting now.  It always goes to the Temple
whatever you have set your own recall to, so a cleric has two places to
reach in a hurry instead of one, and it works while you are cursed,
where the RECALL skill does not.  A scroll or potion of recall carries
the same spell and does the same two things.

@ 20260925y 2026-09-25
Shops take the coins you actually have.  Buying used to look only at the
loose copper in your purse, so a character carrying platinum could be
told they could not afford a loaf of bread.  Shops now make change, and
they pay for what you sell them in coins you can carry.

@ 20260925z 2026-09-25
Prices in low-level areas are priced for low-level characters.  Mud
School sells bread for a copper and a meal for sixteen; a full set of
leather in Dresden is a few gold rather than a few platinum.  Nothing
above level 10 changed.

@ 20260924a 2026-09-24
AQUEST INFO, POINTS, TIME and GAMBLE work wherever you are standing;
only the questmaster's business needs a questmaster.  Every subcommand
can be shortened to its first letter.  Characters under level 4 can be
given a quest at last, and the questmaster now names an area you would
recognise instead of reading out its level range.

@ 20260924b 2026-09-24
REMORT no longer quietly costs you armour.  Gear you keep on through a
remort keeps its bonuses.  Remorting also works if your password has a
capital letter in it, which it did not before.

@ 20260924c 2026-09-24
REPAIR works on gear you are wearing, quotes its price in coins, and
restores an item's armour and worth as well as its condition.

@ 20260924d 2026-09-24
Travel directions to every area in the game are published on the website
at toc.jeremybean.com, and in the Routes panel of the browser client.

@ 20260924e 2026-09-24
Hyrule lets you recall out of it, except from inside the nine dungeons,
and its overworld no longer goes pitch dark at sunset.

@ 20260915a 2026-09-15
Prices are counted in copper.  LIST and APPRAISE write them in the coins
they will cost you - 5g 20s, 1c, free - instead of one long number.

@ 20260915b 2026-09-15
The necromancer's undead line works: CREATE SKELETON, CREATE ZOMBIE and
the rest.  ANIMATE PARTS no longer needs a body part, and hits harder
when it has one.

@ 20260915c 2026-09-15
CAST no longer needs quotes around a spell with a space in its name.

@ 20260915d 2026-09-15
Rooms built in game survive a reboot.
